nodes.body:
Addressed the bitmap-dispatch coverage request in 915e0209f: the public `qsa_forward` test now covers aligned 32K and unaligned packed 32K inputs, empty rows, a row selecting more than 512 blocks, and sampled independent output/LSE references.

The same commit adds the sparse bit-scan compactor for aligned long SM107 rows, retaining the existing fallback and including the helper in cache-source hashing. Frozen-commit QSA validation: 113 passed, 4 skipped; 28 compaction boundary/replay cases pass memory and synchronization checks. The existing toolchain API-probe diagnostic and parent reproduction are documented in the PR body.

@coderabbitai review

